Hi Jim,
Yes, I plan to use a code to remove detection data where covariate data is missing, as is done in the Dynamic occupancy models in unmarked vignette. I want to look at how bat occupancy is affected by my variables (avgextemp in this case) and my understanding was that the code goes as follows
Call:
colext(psiformula = ~1, gammaformula = ~1, epsilonformula = ~1, pformula = ~1, data = Bat, method = "Bat")

I'm interested in the psiformula, which is why I put avgextemp there, not in the pformula or detection. Why do the observation covariates need to be given last?
-Rachel

