MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A zero-inflated abundance distribution might also improve fit (in conjunction with an quadratic or linear trend), although it seems like ideally you'd want the zero-inflation term to vary according to elevation as well (you could do this in the BUGS language).  Of what you've described,  quadratic or polynomial predictors seem like the best way to fit a more irregular response without being forced to make arguments about how specific categories were delineated and why...to me, at least.

