Hi Ivana,

If the probability of being available for detection is simply due to random temporary emigration (as in our 2011 paper), then lambda(i) is the expected super-population size at each transect, and lambda(i)*phi(i,t)/A is the expected density of individuals at transect i on occasion t.

Best,
Richard

